Ours.  Declarations gcc 14 needs in xterm:
each file that called a function with no declaration gets a prototype after its
includes, taken from the definition the call links with (gcc -aux-info).  A K&R
definition's narrow parameters are default-promoted in the prototype, as a K&R caller
passes them (char/short/their typedefs -> int, float -> double):
  programs/xterm/Tekproc.c: set_tek_visibility(Boolean on -> int)
  programs/xterm/button.c: ScrnRefresh(Boolean force -> int)
  programs/xterm/charproc.c: ScrnRefresh(Boolean force -> int); VTReset(Boolean full -> int); unparseputc(char c -> int); set_vt_visibility(Boolean on -> int)
  programs/xterm/input.c: unparseputc(char c -> int)
  programs/xterm/menu.c: set_tek_visibility(Boolean on -> int); VTReset(Boolean full -> int); set_vt_visibility(Boolean on -> int)
  programs/xterm/scrollbar.c: ScrnRefresh(Boolean force -> int)
  programs/xterm/util.c: ScrnRefresh(Boolean force -> int)
Declared without a prototype (types not defined at that point, or called with varying
arguments; none has an ANSI definition with a narrow parameter): Error 

